# What the image build must never see. The Dockerfile itself decides *which* packages ship
# (see its header comment on Collibra/Snowflake); this file's job is the stuff that must never
# reach any image built from this repo, regardless of which Dockerfile stage COPYs what:
# version-control metadata, the governed planning/ bundle, dev-only docs/scripts, every
# package's test suite (including recorded HTTP cassettes), and local tooling/build artifacts.

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# planning/ is a large, separately-governed OKF bundle (CLAUDE.md: "Never hand-edit its
# concepts") with its own hooks, generators, and .venv -- none of it is application code and
# none of it belongs in a runtime image.
planning/

# Repo documentation, dev-only scripts, and root-level docs -- not imported by the engine or
# any of the four packages this image installs.
docs/
scripts/
*.md
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Claude Code / agent tooling config.
.claude/

# Every package's tests: unit tests, fixtures, and recorded vcrpy cassettes. The runtime image
# never imports test code, and cassettes are the single largest dev-only artifact in the repo.
packages/*/tests/

# Python/uv/editor/OS artifacts that must never be baked into a build context.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/.DS_Store
